"Report generation is performed as a queued job, and the job is first checked against a readiness condition. Generation is refused while any student's result in the class is incomplete. A report is a published statement about the class, and a statement that asserts a verdict for a result that is not in is worse than no statement. The refusal is informative rather than merely negative: it reports how many students are complete, how many are pending, which subjects are missing with how many students missing each, and which students are pending, capped at twenty named with the count alongside. A separate readiness check gives the operator the same information before the generate control is used.\n\nGeneration is queued, with an inline fallback when the queue is unavailable so that the job is never lost. The download action regenerates the file afresh from current marks rather than serving a stored copy, and the readiness check therefore runs again at download time. Marks may have been added or withdrawn between queuing and download, and a download must never hand out a sheet stating a verdict for a result that is not in. Scope applies throughout: a branch-scoped member may generate, read, download and delete reports only for their own branches, and deletion is checked against the same scope as reading, otherwise the read scope would be theatre. The complete report bundles seven worksheets — student-wise result, scheme-wise marks, subject analysis, student analysis, class toppers, pass-and-fail analysis and chart data — and every row carries the calculated percentage, the pass verdict, credits earned against total credits and a completeness flag, so the sheet cannot print a verdict the student did not earn.",
